Overview  
This project builds a machine learning model to improve Zomato’s delivery time predictions (ETAs) using real-world operational data. The goal was to reduce delayed orders and convert improved ETA accuracy into measurable business value.  

Key Outcomes:  
- Improved ETA accuracy by 12% (MAE ↓ from 5.7 → 5.0 mins) using Random Forest.  
- Achieved R² = 0.53 through K-Fold Cross Validation.  
- Simulated $7.8M annual revenue uplift from reduced order delays (validated via bootstrapped CI).  

Business Problem  
Inaccurate ETAs frustrate users, increase cancellations, and lower retention.  
Objective: Predict delivery times more accurately to minimize late deliveries and improve customer experience, ultimately driving higher order frequency and revenue.  

Data & Features  
Dataset: [Zomato Delivery Operations Analytics (Kaggle)](https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/saurabhbadole/zomato-delivery-operations-analytics-dataset)  
Size: 45,000+ orders, 20 variables  

Feature Engineering Highlights:
- Spatial: `distance_km` (Haversine formula)  
- Temporal: `day_of_week`, `hour_of_day`, `is_weekend`, cyclical time encoding  
- Operational: `road_traffic_density`, `weather_conditions`, `multiple_deliveries`  
- Custom: `is_delayed` flag — orders delayed >10.2 mins beyond predicted ETA  

Modeling  
Algorithms:  
- Linear Regression (Baseline)  
- Random Forest Regressor (500 trees)  

Evaluation Metrics: MAE (primary), RMSE, R²  

| Model | MAE ↓ | RMSE ↓ | R² ↑ |  
|-------|--------|--------|------|  
| Linear Regression | 5.70 | 7.14 | 0.42 |  
| Random Forest | 5.00 | 6.39 | 0.53 |  

Business Simulation:
- Delay rate reduced from **7.07% → 2.82%**  
- Revenue uplift: $0.017 per order ≈ $7.8M annually  
- 95% CI validated through bootstrapping  

Business Impact  
Improving ETA accuracy drives measurable ROI:  
- Fewer delayed orders → improved customer satisfaction & retention  
- Translating model improvement into order frequency uplift
- Proposed A/B testing and biweekly retraining for production deployment  

